//@version=6
indicator("Polaris Scanner — Sweep / CISD / FVG / ICT", overlay=true, max_lines_count=200, max_boxes_count=150, max_labels_count=250)

// ============================================================================
// Polaris Scanner (Pine port) + ICT confluence markup
// Core model matches Polaris's JS scanner (advanceScan/findSwings/fvgAt in
// index.html): liquidity sweep -> change in state of delivery (CISD) ->
// retrace into the resulting fair value gap -> rejection. On a completed
// setup, fires a webhook alert shaped for the Polaris receiveAlert Cloud
// Function (see functions/index.js). That core logic is unchanged below.
//
// Everything else on the chart is confluence markup, independent of the
// alert-firing state machine: order blocks, every significant fair value gap
// (flipped to iFVG styling once violated, deleted once reclaimed), equal
// highs/lows (liquidity pools -- the ONLY swings the scanner will treat as
// sweepable; lone/unmatched swings are ignored as noise), a premium/discount
// zone around the active swing range, and killzone session shading. Each has
// its own show/hide toggle. Colors match Polaris's own dark cyan/gold
// command-center theme:
//   cyan   #00D4FF  -- structure / tracking (level line, entry line, HUD)
//   gold   #F5C86B  -- attention (sweeps, liquidity pools, iFVG flips)
//   green  #2FE08A  -- bullish / long bias
//   red    #FF5566  -- bearish / short bias
//
// Entry/stop/target/confidence are NOT part of the original JS scanner
// model (it only annotates structure, no trade parameters) -- these are
// invented here specifically for the webhook payload:
//   stop       = the sweep's actual extreme (the protected level -- not just
//                the old swing price it swept) +/- an optional buffer
//   target     = the nearest untested liquidity pool in the trade's
//                direction (a real draw of liquidity, findLiquidityTarget)
//                -- falls back to entry +/- risk * rMultiple only when no
//                pool exists yet. A setup only actually alerts if that
//                projected move clears BOTH minTargetAtrMult x ATR(14) AND
//                minTargetPts (a flat, ATR-independent point floor -- a
//                quiet-market ATR compression can satisfy the ATR-relative
//                check on a handful of points alone, which is how a real
//                4-point NQ alert got through; the two gates are ANDed so
//                neither one alone can let a too-small move fire);
//                smaller draws still resolve the sequence, they just don't
//                fire a webhook.
//   confidence = FVG size relative to ATR(14) blended with volume strength
//                relative to its own recent average, a rough heuristic only
// Adjust the inputs below, or the setupConfidence()/findLiquidityTarget()
// formulas, to taste.
//
// Three more filters gate whether a sweep is even allowed to start a
// sequence: a higher-timeframe bias check (HTF close vs its own EMA, via
// request.security -- no short setups while the HTF is bullish and vice
// versa), a market-regime check (ta.dmi's ADX -- no new setups while the
// market is chopping, below the ADX threshold), and an optional session
// filter (useSessionFilter -- no new setups outside the Asia/London/NY AM/
// NY PM killzones once enabled). Volume is deliberately NOT a gate -- it
// only ever informs the confidence score (see setupConfidence below), so
// every setup still fires and you can judge its volume strength yourself.
// Pine has no access to real bid/ask or DOM data -- the volume figure used
// there is bar volume vs its own recent average, not true order flow, but
// it's the closest proxy available. Pine indicators also cannot call an
// LLM/API in real time (no such capability exists in the sandbox --
// alert() is a one-way webhook fire, nothing reads a response back into
// the script), so these are the ways this indicator can be genuinely
// "market aware" on its own. Deeper judgment from Polaris's actual Claude
// brain happens downstream instead, in index.html, once an alert reaches
// the dashboard.
//
// Two kinds of webhook payloads go out, discriminated by a "kind" field the
// Cloud Function branches on: "setup" (buildAlertMessage) fires once, on a
// fully completed setup, and gets AI-reviewed on the dashboard. "status"
// (buildStatusMessage) fires on every phase advance (sweep detected -> CISD
// confirmed -> retracing) with the indicator's current bias/HTF/regime/phase
// -- a lightweight, constantly-overwritten "what am I watching right now"
// ping, not stored history, so Polaris can speak up mid-sequence instead of
// only ever hearing about a setup once it's already done.
//
// A built-in scorecard tracks every fired setup until price actually trades
// through its stop or target, tallying wins/losses on the HUD ("SCORE").
// Since Pine replays the whole script over all available chart history on
// every load, this isn't just forward-tracking -- it's a real backtest of
// the current rule set the moment you paste this in, not something you
// have to wait days to accumulate.
//
// V2 rework: all five original problems are now addressed, though not all
// equally battle-tested -- see the note at the very end of this block.
//   1. Signal contradiction -- useContradictionFilter/minBarsAfterSetup
//      block a new setup within minBarsAfterSetup of the last one that
//      actually fired in the opposite direction (lastSetupDir/
//      lastSetupBar), checked in shouldFireSetup(). Only
//      useContradictionFilter=false disables it.
//   2. Coverage gaps -- detectReversal() (any swing break, not just a
//      pool-eligible one), detectContinuation() (a with-trend pullback on
//      a fresh displacement candle while structureBias already agrees),
//      and detectBreakout() (a displacement close beyond the widest
//      tracked swing on that side) are real now, tried in that order after
//      detectSweep() on every bar with no active sequence. Each is
//      independently gated by allowSweep/allowReversal/allowContinuation/
//      allowBreakout -- only allowSweep defaults on, so nothing changes
//      until you opt the others in. Whichever detector actually triggers
//      is reported as the webhook's setupType via setupTypeForTrigger()
//      (sweep -> LIQUIDITY_SWEEP_*, reversal -> CHoCH_*, continuation and
//      breakout -> BOS_*, reusing functions/index.js's existing allow-list).
//   3. Fragile stop -- useWickTolerance/wickToleranceAtr widen the stop
//      beyond the sweep's actual wick by an ATR-scaled buffer, at all 4
//      completion sites. This widens where the stop SITS; it does not
//      pretend a real touched stop wouldn't fill -- that would misrepresent
//      real broker/order-fill behavior, so there's no "grace period" logic.
//   4. Generic TP fallback -- unchanged from the earlier liquidity-pool
//      targeting pass (computeTarget()/findLiquidityTarget()); still
//      reports targetSource so the dashboard can explain which it used.
//   5. No visual guidance -- solved in an earlier pass (buildTradePlanDrawings);
//      showTradePlan now independently controls it (used to just mirror
//      showVisuals, which still separately controls the sweep/CISD-in-
//      progress markup), and showTpLadder optionally adds TP1/TP2 lines at
//      50%/75% of the distance to the final target -- purely visual, the
//      webhook payload/scorecard/target still resolve against the one real
//      target regardless.
// Plus two general signal-quality floors, also live: raiseAdxThreshold/
// raisedAdxThreshold (stricter ADX minimum), useVolFloor/volFloorMult (min
// volume ratio), minBarRangeAtr (reject a dead/illiquid confirmation bar),
// and minSeqFvgSizeAtr (reject a too-small confirming FVG) -- all checked
// in shouldFireSetup() except minSeqFvgSizeAtr, which depends on that
// specific sequence's FVG and is checked at the 4 completion sites instead.
// Every new gate defaults to a value that roughly reproduces prior
// behavior (raiseAdxThreshold/useVolFloor off, minBarRangeAtr/
// minSeqFvgSizeAtr low/zero) so this pass doesn't quietly starve you of
// signals -- turn them up deliberately to actually tighten things.
//
// Two more real gates, prompted directly by a live 4-point NQ alert and its
// follow-up review: minTargetPts (grpTrade) is an unconditional floor on the
// projected move in raw instrument points, ANDed with the existing
// minTargetAtrMult check -- a quiet-market ATR compression could satisfy "3x
// ATR" on a handful of points alone, which is exactly how that alert got
// through; now both gates must pass. minRiskReward (grpTrade) is a genuine
// floor on reward/risk itself, checked at all 4 completion sites -- riskReward
// was already computed and reported in the webhook payload, but nothing
// actually gated on it, so a setup could clear both size floors while still
// carrying a disproportionately wide stop.
//
// Liquidity-pool significance (grpEQ): Swing now tracks touches (how many
// swings have clustered at that price zone, starting at 1), not just a bare
// isPool boolean. Sweep-eligibility (detectSweep/detectReversal) is
// unchanged -- still fires on the first match (touches=2). But
// findLiquidityTarget() (the real TARGET) and the new findLiquidityLevels()
// (TP1/TP2) now require touches >= minPoolTouches, so "target" doesn't
// default to meaning "the nearest level that barely qualified once." The
// TP1/TP2 ladder itself is also no longer arbitrary 50%/75% splits of the
// distance to target -- it now draws the nearest one or two REAL liquidity
// pools actually sitting between entry and target, drawing fewer than two
// lines rather than fabricating a percentage-based one if that's all that
// exists in range.
//
// SMT divergence (grpSMT): pulls pivot highs/lows from a correlated symbol
// (smtSymbol, default the E-mini S&P) at the identical pivot cadence, so a
// confirmed pivot here lines up bar-for-bar with one there -- no separate
// swing-tracking state needed for the other symbol. Bearish divergence =
// we make a higher high the correlated symbol doesn't confirm; bullish is
// the mirror at lows. Captured once, at sweep/reversal/continuation/
// breakout trigger time (seqSmtAligned), and blended into setupConfidence()
// alongside FVG size and volume -- informational only, like volume, never a
// gate.
//
// Dashboard integration additions: buildAlertMessage() also reports
// "targetSource" ("pool" if computeTarget() found a real untested liquidity
// pool, "fallback" if it fell back to the R-multiple projection instead) --
// this is what lets Polaris explain, not just display, why a given target
// sits where it does. buildStatusMessage() also carries the live
// scoreWins/scoreLosses tally on every ping, so the dashboard's win-rate
// reading stays current without waiting for the next full setup to fire.
//
// A note on the new entry triggers: reversal/continuation/breakout are
// real, working implementations, but -- unlike detectSweep(), which mirrors
// the original JS model this whole indicator was ported from -- they're
// this author's own reasonable-but-invented interpretation of those ICT
// concepts, not something battle-tested against the original model. They
// default OFF (allowReversal/allowContinuation/allowBreakout) specifically
// so turning each on is a deliberate choice, and the scorecard will tell
// you fairly quickly whether a given one is actually pulling its weight.
//
// Multi-timeframe framework (grpHTF/grpDirection/grpM1): a top-down, four-layer
// read instead of everything happening on one timeframe.
//   1H  BIAS      -- useHtfBias/htfTimeframe (existing, unchanged): HTF close vs
//                    its own EMA, gates counter-bias setups.
//   15m DIRECTION -- useMtfDirection/directionTimeframe (new): structureBias
//                    itself gets re-sourced from a dedicated timeframe's pivots
//                    (dirPh/dirPl via request.security, compared against
//                    dirPrevHigh/dirPrevLow the same way SMT compares its own
//                    pivot pair) instead of the chart's own swings. Off ->
//                    structureBias reverts to exactly the old chart-native
//                    behavior. This is a GATE, same as bias always was --
//                    shouldFireSetup()'s biasOk check is unchanged, it just now
//                    reads a structureBias sourced from 15m instead of 5m.
//   5m  STATE     -- unchanged: the sweep/CISD/retrace sequence tracker below
//                    still runs on whatever timeframe the chart itself is on.
//   1m  ENTRIES   -- useM1Confirmation (new): the most recently confirmed
//                    1-minute candle's OHLC (m1o/m1h/m1l/m1c via
//                    request.security), reduced to a simple long-wick rejection
//                    read (m1RejectionBear/m1RejectionBull) and folded into
//                    setupConfidence() as one more sub-score. Deliberately
//                    informational only, never a gate -- stacking a fourth
//                    mandatory confluence layer on top of bias/direction/state
//                    risked strangling an already-infrequent signal further.
// All three request.security pulls (HTF, direction, 1m) run unconditionally
// every bar regardless of their toggles, same CW10003 reasoning as the
// pre-existing htfClose/htfEma/SMT pulls.
// ============================================================================

// ---------- inputs ----------
grpScan = "Scanner"
swingStrength = input.int(3, "Swing strength (bars each side)", minval=1, maxval=10, group=grpScan)
maxBarsValid  = input.int(40, "Max bars before a sequence expires", minval=5, group=grpScan)
maxSwings     = input.int(20, "Max recent swings tracked per side", minval=5, maxval=50, group=grpScan)
showVisuals   = input.bool(true, "Show sweep/CISD/trade-plan markup", group=grpScan)
showHud       = input.bool(true, "Show status panel (top-right)", group=grpScan)

grpTrade = "Trade parameters (for the webhook payload only)"
stopBufferPts     = input.float(0.0, "Stop buffer beyond the sweep extreme (points)", minval=0, group=grpTrade)
rMultiple         = input.float(2.0, "Fallback target R-multiple (only used if no liquidity pool sits in the trade's direction)", minval=0.1, group=grpTrade)
minTargetAtrMult  = input.float(3.0, "Min projected move to actually alert (x ATR) -- smaller draws complete the sequence but don't fire", minval=0, step=0.5, group=grpTrade)
// ATR-relative alone isn't enough -- a genuinely quiet stretch (thin holiday session,
// low-liquidity overnight hours) can compress ATR far enough that "3x ATR" is satisfied
// by a handful of points, which is how a real 4-point NQ alert got through on the 5m
// chart. This is a second, unconditional floor in raw instrument points -- both gates
// must pass, so a quiet market can no longer talk its way around the ATR check.
minTargetPts      = input.float(20.0, "Absolute minimum projected move to alert (points, instrument-native -- independent of ATR)", minval=0, step=1, group=grpTrade)
// riskReward is already computed and reported in the webhook payload, but nothing
// actually gated on it -- a setup could clear both size floors above while still
// carrying a disproportionately wide stop (e.g. a 25pt reward on an 80pt risk),
// which is arguably a worse trade than the tiny-reward problem those floors fix.
// This is a genuine, unconditional minimum on reward/risk itself, checked
// alongside them at all 4 completion sites (0 disables, same pattern as the
// other "0 disables" gates in this file).
minRiskReward     = input.float(1.5, "Min risk:reward to alert (reward/risk, 0 disables)", minval=0, step=0.1, group=grpTrade)

grpHook = "Webhook"
webhookSecret = input.string("", "Webhook secret (must match WEBHOOK_SECRET)", group=grpHook)

grpFVG = "Fair Value Gaps"
showAllFvg    = input.bool(true, "Mark every significant FVG on the chart", group=grpFVG)
showIfvg      = input.bool(true, "Flip violated FVGs to iFVG styling", group=grpFVG)
minFvgSizeAtr = input.float(0.3, "Min FVG size to mark (x ATR)", minval=0, step=0.05, group=grpFVG)
maxFvgBoxes   = input.int(15, "Max FVG boxes shown", minval=1, maxval=50, group=grpFVG)

grpOB = "Order Blocks"
showOB       = input.bool(true, "Mark order blocks", group=grpOB)
obBiasFilter = input.bool(true, "Only mark order blocks agreeing with the standing bias", group=grpOB)
dispMult     = input.float(2.0, "Displacement threshold (x ATR)", minval=0.5, step=0.1, group=grpOB)
obLookback   = input.int(3, "Bars back to find the opposing candle", minval=1, maxval=8, group=grpOB)
maxOB        = input.int(12, "Max order blocks shown", minval=1, maxval=40, group=grpOB)

grpEQ = "Equal Highs / Lows"
showEQ   = input.bool(true, "Mark equal highs/lows (liquidity pools)", group=grpEQ)
eqTolPct = input.float(0.05, "Equal tolerance (% of price)", minval=0.01, step=0.01, group=grpEQ)
// sweep-eligibility (isPool, used by detectSweep/detectReversal) is untouched by this --
// it still fires on the first match, same as always. This only raises the bar for what
// counts as a real TARGET/TP: a level barely qualifying on one match isn't necessarily
// meaningful liquidity, vs. one multiple prior swings have actually clustered at.
minPoolTouches = input.int(2, "Min touches for a level to count as a real target/TP (2 = first equal-high/low match, same as before; raise for more established levels only)", minval=2, maxval=6, group=grpEQ)

grpPD = "Premium / Discount"
showPD = input.bool(false, "Shade premium/discount zone", group=grpPD)

grpKZ = "Killzones (New York time)"
showKillzones       = input.bool(false, "Shade killzone sessions", group=grpKZ)
useSessionFilter    = input.bool(false, "Only allow new setups during a killzone session", group=grpKZ)
showSessionVolatility = input.bool(true, "Track average range per session on the HUD", group=grpKZ)
asiaSession   = input.session("2000-0000", "Asia killzone", group=grpKZ)
londonSession = input.session("0200-0500", "London killzone", group=grpKZ)
nyAmSession   = input.session("0930-1100", "NY AM killzone", group=grpKZ)
nyPmSession   = input.session("1330-1600", "NY PM killzone", group=grpKZ)

grpHTF = "Higher Timeframe Bias"
useHtfBias   = input.bool(true, "Require higher-timeframe agreement", group=grpHTF)
htfTimeframe = input.timeframe("60", "Higher timeframe", group=grpHTF)
htfEmaLen    = input.int(50, "HTF EMA length", minval=5, group=grpHTF)

// ---------- multi-timeframe framework ----------
// Four layers, top-down: 1H bias (grpHTF above), 15m direction (this group --
// structureBias itself, normally sourced from whatever timeframe the chart is
// on, gets re-sourced from a dedicated higher timeframe instead), 5m current
// state (the sweep/CISD/retrace sequence tracker below -- unchanged, still
// runs on whatever timeframe the chart is actually on), and 1m entries (next
// group -- a finer-grained rejection-candle read folded into confidence only,
// never a gate, so it can't choke signal frequency on top of the other three
// layers).
grpDirection = "Direction (structure-bias timeframe)"
useMtfDirection    = input.bool(true, "Source structure bias/direction from a dedicated timeframe instead of the chart's own swings", group=grpDirection)
directionTimeframe = input.timeframe("15", "Direction timeframe", group=grpDirection)

grpM1 = "1-Minute Entry Confirmation"
useM1Confirmation = input.bool(true, "Factor a 1-minute rejection-candle read into confidence score (never blocks a signal)", group=grpM1)

grpRegime = "Market Regime"
useRegimeFilter = input.bool(true, "Only scan when the market is trending (ADX filter)", group=grpRegime)
adxLen          = input.int(14, "ADX length", minval=2, group=grpRegime)
adxThreshold    = input.float(20, "Min ADX to allow new setups", minval=5, maxval=50, group=grpRegime)

grpScore = "Scorecard"
showScorecard = input.bool(true, "Track win rate on the HUD", group=grpScore)
maxPending    = input.int(50, "Max pending signals tracked at once", minval=5, maxval=200, group=grpScore)

grpVolume = "Volume"
useVolumeConfirm = input.bool(true, "Factor volume strength into confidence score (never blocks a signal)", group=grpVolume)
volAvgLen = input.int(20, "Volume average length", minval=5, group=grpVolume)

// ---------- V2 groundwork + Phase 2 gates ----------
// All four setup types are real, working implementations now (see the
// detect*() functions below, filled in during V2 Phase 3) -- reversal/
// continuation/breakout default OFF not because they're unimplemented, but
// because they're this author's own interpretation of those ICT concepts
// rather than something ported from the original JS model the way sweep is
// (see the header note above), so turning each on is meant to be a
// deliberate, individually-scrutinized choice. Everything under
// grpGates/grpMemory/grpSL is now live, checked by shouldFireSetup()
// (and, for minSeqFvgSizeAtr and the wick-tolerant stop buffer, at the 4
// completion sites directly) -- all default to values that roughly
// reproduce Phase 1's behavior (raiseAdxThreshold/useVolFloor default off,
// minBarRangeAtr/minSeqFvgSizeAtr default low/zero), so this pass doesn't
// suddenly starve you of signals, but every gate is now real, not cosmetic.
grpSetups = "Setup Types"
allowSweep        = input.bool(true, "Allow sweep-based setups", group=grpSetups)
allowReversal     = input.bool(false, "Allow reversal-based setups (author's own ICT interpretation -- see header note)", group=grpSetups)
allowContinuation = input.bool(false, "Allow continuation-based setups (author's own ICT interpretation -- see header note)", group=grpSetups)
allowBreakout     = input.bool(false, "Allow breakout-based setups (author's own ICT interpretation -- see header note)", group=grpSetups)

grpGates = "Signal Quality Gates"
useVolFloor       = input.bool(false, "Require a minimum volume ratio to fire", group=grpGates)
volFloorMult      = input.float(0.8, "Min volume ratio if the floor above is enabled", minval=0, step=0.1, group=grpGates)
raiseAdxThreshold = input.bool(false, "Require a stricter ADX minimum than the Market Regime setting", group=grpGates)
raisedAdxThreshold = input.float(30, "Stricter ADX minimum, used only if the toggle above is on", minval=5, maxval=60, group=grpGates)
minBarRangeAtr    = input.float(0.15, "Min bar range to trust as signal context, x ATR (0 disables)", minval=0, step=0.05, group=grpGates)
minSeqFvgSizeAtr  = input.float(0.0, "Min size of a sequence's own confirming FVG, x ATR (0 disables)", minval=0, step=0.05, group=grpGates)

grpMemory = "Contradiction Memory"
useContradictionFilter = input.bool(true, "Block a new setup that directly contradicts one just fired", group=grpMemory)
minBarsAfterSetup      = input.int(10, "Min bars after a completed setup before the opposite direction can fire", minval=0, group=grpMemory)

grpSL = "Wick-Tolerant Stops"
useWickTolerance  = input.bool(true, "Widen the stop beyond the sweep wick so a single spike can't take it out", group=grpSL)
wickToleranceAtr  = input.float(0.25, "Extra stop buffer beyond the sweep's wick, x ATR", minval=0, step=0.05, group=grpSL)

grpVisualsV2 = "Trade Plan Visuals"
showTradePlan  = input.bool(true, "Show entry/stop/target trade-plan markup (independent of the sweep/CISD markup toggle above)", group=grpVisualsV2)
lineExtension  = input.int(15, "Trade-plan line length (bars)", minval=1, maxval=60, group=grpVisualsV2)
showTpLadder   = input.bool(false, "Also draw TP1/TP2 lines at 50%/75% of the distance to the final target", group=grpVisualsV2)
showConfidence = input.bool(true, "Show the confidence % on the setup label", group=grpVisualsV2)

grpSMT = "SMT Divergence"
useSmtConfluence = input.bool(true, "Factor SMT divergence into confidence score (never blocks a signal)", group=grpSMT)
smtSymbol        = input.symbol("CME_MINI:ES1!", "Correlated symbol to compare swing points against", group=grpSMT)

// ---------- types ----------
type Swing
    int   idx
    float price
    bool  isPool  // true once this swing clusters with another (an equal high/low) -- only pool swings are sweep-eligible
    int   touches // how many swings (including this one) have clustered at this price zone -- starts at 1, rises with each further match. Sweep-eligibility (isPool) still fires on the first match (touches=2) unchanged; target/TP selection can require a stricter minPoolTouches so "target" doesn't mean "the nearest barely-qualifying level"

// ---------- persistent state: core scanner ----------
var array<Swing> swingHighs = array.new<Swing>()
var array<Swing> swingLows  = array.new<Swing>()

// standing directional filter, independent of the sweep/CISD scanner --
// a higher high / higher low sets it bullish, a lower high / lower low sets
// it bearish. The scanner only starts sequences that agree with it, so a
// bull bias won't fire short setups until structure actually breaks bearish.
var string structureBias = na   // "bull" | "bear"

var string seqDir        = na   // "bull" | "bear"
var string seqPhase      = na   // "sweep" | "cisd" | "retrace"
var float  seqLevel      = na
var float  seqCisdTarget = na
var int    seqSweepBar   = na
var bool   seqHasFvg     = false
var float  seqFvgLo      = na
var float  seqFvgHi      = na
var float  seqSweepExtreme = na  // actual high/low the sweep candle reached -- the real "protected" level, stop lives beyond this, not just beyond the old swing price
var bool   seqSmtAligned = false  // SMT reading captured at sweep time, not re-read later -- see setupConfidence()
var string seqTriggerType = na    // "sweep" | "reversal" | "continuation" | "breakout" -- which detector actually started this sequence, mapped to a webhook setupType at completion

// last setup that actually fired a webhook (not just completed the
// sequence) -- what useContradictionFilter checks against, so a quiet
// completion (below minTargetAtrMult/minSeqFvgSizeAtr) never blocks a
// future opposite-direction signal.
var string lastSetupDir = na   // "bull" | "bear"
var int    lastSetupBar = na

// SMT divergence tracking -- smtPrevHigh/smtPrevLow remember the correlated
// symbol's own last confirmed pivot so the next one can be compared against
// it; smtBearDiv/smtBullDiv are set the moment our own swing confirms (see
// the swing-detection block below) and read once, at whichever completion
// site fires next, by setupConfidence().
var float smtPrevHigh = na
var float smtPrevLow  = na
var bool  smtBearDiv  = false
var bool  smtBullDiv  = false

// Direction (15m by default) tracking -- same pattern as the SMT pair above:
// dirPrevHigh/dirPrevLow remember the direction timeframe's own last confirmed
// pivot so the next one can be compared against it, updating structureBias
// directly (see the swing-detection block below) when useMtfDirection is on.
var float dirPrevHigh = na
var float dirPrevLow  = na

// ---------- persistent state: trade-plan markup (single most recent completed setup) ----------
var line  tpEntryLine = na
var line  tpStopLine  = na
var line  tpTargetLine = na
var line  tp1Line     = na  // TP-ladder lines (showTpLadder) -- na/unused unless the toggle is on
var line  tp2Line     = na
var label tpEntryLbl  = na
var label tpStopLbl   = na
var label tpTargetLbl = na
var label tp1Lbl      = na
var label tp2Lbl      = na
var label tpSetupLbl  = na
var string tpDir      = na   // "bull" | "bear" -- direction of the tracked plan
var float  tpStop     = na
var float  tpTarget   = na
var bool   tpActive   = false

// ---------- persistent state: confluence markup ----------
var array<box> fvgBoxes     = array.new<box>()
var array<float> fvgBoxLo   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> fvgBoxHi   = array.new<float>()
var array<string> fvgBoxDir = array.new<string>()
var array<bool> fvgBoxDone  = array.new<bool>()
var array<box> obBoxes      = array.new<box>()
var box premiumBox = na
var box discountBox = na
var line eqLine = na

// ---------- persistent state: scorecard ----------
// every fired setup gets recorded here until price actually trades through
// its stop or target; tallied into scoreWins/scoreLosses once resolved.
// Pine replays this over the whole visible chart history on every reload,
// so this reflects a real backtest under the current rules, not just
// signals fired since you last opened the chart.
// sumR is why win% alone is the wrong number to judge this by: every fired
// setup already clears minRiskReward, so a loss always costs exactly -1R
// (it resolves at the stop) but a win pays out whatever THAT trade's real
// reward:risk was, not a fixed amount. A 35% win rate at 3R average beats
// a 65% win rate at 1.2R average. sumR / (wins+losses) is real expectancy
// in R-multiples -- the number that actually says whether this is working.
var array<string> pendingDir    = array.new<string>()
var array<float> pendingEntry   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> pendingStop    = array.new<float>()
var array<float> pendingTarget  = array.new<float>()
var int scoreWins   = 0
var int scoreLosses = 0
var float sumR      = 0.0

// ---------- persistent state: per-session volatility ----------
// running average of each killzone's realized range (high-low across the
// whole session), folded in the moment a session ends -- not a signal
// filter, just an "how much does this session actually move" readout.
var string curSession     = na
var float  curSessionHigh = na
var float  curSessionLow  = na
var float  sumRangeAsia   = 0.0
var int    countAsia      = 0
var float  sumRangeLondon = 0.0
var int    countLondon    = 0
var float  sumRangeNyAm   = 0.0
var int    countNyAm      = 0
var float  sumRangeNyPm   = 0.0
var int    countNyPm      = 0

// ---------- swing detection (mirrors findSwings) + equal highs/lows ----------
ph = ta.pivothigh(swingStrength, swingStrength)
pl = ta.pivotlow(swingStrength, swingStrength)

// SMT divergence source: pulled from a correlated symbol at the identical
// pivot cadence (same swingStrength, same timeframe), so a confirmed pivot
// here lines up bar-for-bar with a confirmed pivot there -- no separate
// swing-tracking state needed for the other symbol.
smtPh = request.security(smtSymbol, timeframe.period, ta.pivothigh(swingStrength, swingStrength))
smtPl = request.security(smtSymbol, timeframe.period, ta.pivotlow(swingStrength, swingStrength))

// Direction source: same pivot function pulled from a dedicated timeframe (15m by
// default) instead of a correlated symbol -- called unconditionally every bar
// regardless of useMtfDirection, matching the smtPh/smtPl pattern above (a
// request.security call gated by an if-block trips Pine's CW10003 warning).
dirPh = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, directionTimeframe, ta.pivothigh(swingStrength, swingStrength))
dirPl = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, directionTimeframe, ta.pivotlow(swingStrength, swingStrength))

if not na(ph)
    int newHighIdx = bar_index - swingStrength
    // pool-matching runs unconditionally (it decides which swings are sweep-eligible
    // liquidity pools) -- showEQ only controls whether the match gets drawn. Also
    // tracks how many swings have now clustered at this zone (matchTouches), so
    // target/TP selection can later prefer well-established levels over a level
    // that just barely qualified on its first match.
    bool poolMatch = false
    int matchTouches = 1
    if array.size(swingHighs) > 0
        float tol = ph * eqTolPct / 100
        for i = 0 to array.size(swingHighs) - 1
            Swing s = array.get(swingHighs, i)
            if math.abs(s.price - ph) <= tol
                poolMatch := true
                s.isPool := true
                s.touches := s.touches + 1
                matchTouches := s.touches
                if showEQ
                    line.new(s.idx, s.price, newHighIdx, ph, color=color.new(#F5C86B, 30), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
                    label.new(newHighIdx, ph, "EQH", style=label.style_label_down, color=color.new(#0B1626, 15), textcolor=#F5C86B, size=size.tiny)
                break
    if array.size(swingHighs) > 0
        Swing prevHigh = array.get(swingHighs, 0)
        if ph > prevHigh.price
            // structureBias only set from the chart's own swings when useMtfDirection
            // is off -- otherwise the dedicated direction-timeframe block below owns it
            if not useMtfDirection
                structureBias := "bull"
            // bearish SMT: we made a higher high, the correlated symbol didn't
            smtBearDiv := not na(smtPh) and not na(smtPrevHigh) and smtPh <= smtPrevHigh
        else if ph < prevHigh.price
            if not useMtfDirection
                structureBias := "bear"
    if not na(smtPh)
        smtPrevHigh := smtPh
    array.unshift(swingHighs, Swing.new(newHighIdx, ph, poolMatch, matchTouches))
    if array.size(swingHighs) > maxSwings
        array.pop(swingHighs)

if not na(pl)
    int newLowIdx = bar_index - swingStrength
    bool poolMatchLow = false
    int matchTouchesLow = 1
    if array.size(swingLows) > 0
        float tol = pl * eqTolPct / 100
        for i = 0 to array.size(swingLows) - 1
            Swing s = array.get(swingLows, i)
            if math.abs(s.price - pl) <= tol
                poolMatchLow := true
                s.isPool := true
                s.touches := s.touches + 1
                matchTouchesLow := s.touches
                if showEQ
                    line.new(s.idx, s.price, newLowIdx, pl, color=color.new(#F5C86B, 30), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
                    label.new(newLowIdx, pl, "EQL", style=label.style_label_up, color=color.new(#0B1626, 15), textcolor=#F5C86B, size=size.tiny)
                break
    if array.size(swingLows) > 0
        Swing prevLow = array.get(swingLows, 0)
        if pl < prevLow.price
            if not useMtfDirection
                structureBias := "bear"
            // bullish SMT: we made a lower low, the correlated symbol didn't
            smtBullDiv := not na(smtPl) and not na(smtPrevLow) and smtPl >= smtPrevLow
        else if pl > prevLow.price
            if not useMtfDirection
                structureBias := "bull"
    if not na(smtPl)
        smtPrevLow := smtPl
    array.unshift(swingLows, Swing.new(newLowIdx, pl, poolMatchLow, matchTouchesLow))
    if array.size(swingLows) > maxSwings
        array.pop(swingLows)

// direction-timeframe structure bias -- only when useMtfDirection is on. Updates
// independently of the chart's own ph/pl pivots above, since a 15m pivot confirms
// on its own schedule, not bar-for-bar with the chart's 5m swings. Same
// higher-high/higher-low vs lower-high/lower-low logic as the chart-native version,
// just comparing the direction timeframe's own last two confirmed pivots.
if useMtfDirection
    if not na(dirPh)
        if not na(dirPrevHigh)
            structureBias := dirPh > dirPrevHigh ? "bull" : dirPh < dirPrevHigh ? "bear" : structureBias
        dirPrevHigh := dirPh
    if not na(dirPl)
        if not na(dirPrevLow)
            structureBias := dirPl < dirPrevLow ? "bear" : dirPl > dirPrevLow ? "bull" : structureBias
        dirPrevLow := dirPl

// ---------- helpers ----------
// mirrors cisdTargetBear/Bull(cs, idx) -- only ever called at idx == current
// bar (offset 0), i.e. right when a sweep is first detected this bar.
cisdTargetBear() =>
    int j = 0
    if close[j] <= open[j]
        j := j + 1
    int start = -1
    while j <= 200 and close[j] > open[j]
        start := j
        j := j + 1
    start >= 0 ? open[start] : low[0]

cisdTargetBull() =>
    int j = 0
    if close[j] >= open[j]
        j := j + 1
    int start = -1
    while j <= 200 and close[j] < open[j]
        start := j
        j := j + 1
    start >= 0 ? open[start] : high[0]

// mirrors fvgAt(cs, k, dir) -- off is bars back from current bar for candle "k"
fvgAtBear(int off) =>
    bool has = low[off + 2] > high[off]
    [has, has ? high[off] : na, has ? low[off + 2] : na]

fvgAtBull(int off) =>
    bool has = high[off + 2] < low[off]
    [has, has ? high[off + 2] : na, has ? low[off] : na]

// atrVal, htfBias and adxVal must all be computed unconditionally every bar --
// ta.*/request.security calls inside a function or if-block that's only
// invoked conditionally trip Pine's CW10003 warning.
atrVal = ta.atr(14)

// higher-timeframe bias -- HTF close above/below its own EMA. Repaint-safe:
// lookahead is off, so this only ever reflects the last *closed* HTF bar.
htfClose = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTimeframe, close, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
htfEma   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTimeframe, ta.ema(close, htfEmaLen), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
string htfBias = htfClose > htfEma ? "bull" : htfClose < htfEma ? "bear" : na

// market regime -- ADX below threshold means chop/no clear trend
[diPlus, diMinus, adxVal] = ta.dmi(adxLen, adxLen)
bool regimeOk = not useRegimeFilter or adxVal >= adxThreshold

// 1-minute entry read: the most recently confirmed 1m candle's OHLC, pulled
// unconditionally every bar (same CW10003 reasoning as htfClose/htfEma above).
// A long wick relative to the candle's own range is a simple, defensible
// rejection-leg proxy -- informational only (see grpM1/useM1Confirmation),
// folded into setupConfidence(), never a gate, so it can't choke signal
// frequency on top of the 1H bias / 15m direction / 5m state gates.
[m1o, m1h, m1l, m1c] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1", [open, high, low, close], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
float m1Range = m1h - m1l
bool m1RejectionBear = m1Range > 0 and (m1h - math.max(m1o, m1c)) > m1Range * 0.5
bool m1RejectionBull = m1Range > 0 and (math.min(m1o, m1c) - m1l) > m1Range * 0.5

// declared here (not down by the order-block section it was originally
// written for) because detectContinuation()/detectBreakout() below also
// need it, and Pine requires an identifier declared above the code that
// reads it -- same lesson as the killzone-block move earlier in this file.
bool isDisplacement = math.abs(close - open) > atrVal * dispMult

// order flow proxy -- Pine has no access to real bid/ask or DOM data, so
// this is bar volume vs its own recent average, not true order flow.
// Informational only: folded into the confidence score below and shown on
// the HUD, but never blocks a sweep or CISD from firing.
avgVolume = ta.sma(volume, volAvgLen)
float volRatio = avgVolume > 0 ? volume / avgVolume : na

// heuristic only, not predictive -- averages whichever 30-95 sub-scores are
// currently enabled: FVG size relative to recent volatility (always in),
// volume strength relative to its own recent average (if useVolumeConfirm),
// and SMT divergence agreement (if useSmtConfluence, using the reading
// captured at sweep time -- see seqSmtAligned). None of these ever block a
// signal from firing; they're only ever ingredients in the confidence
// number, not gates.
setupConfidence(float fvgLo, float fvgHi, float atr, float volRatioNow, bool smtAligned, bool m1Aligned) =>
    float size = fvgHi - fvgLo
    float sizeRatio = atr > 0 ? size / atr : 0
    int sizeScore = math.round(math.max(30, math.min(95, 40 + sizeRatio * 40)))
    float vr = na(volRatioNow) ? 1.0 : volRatioNow
    int volScore = math.round(math.max(30, math.min(95, 40 + vr * 30)))
    int smtScore = smtAligned ? 90 : 60
    int m1Score = m1Aligned ? 90 : 55
    float sum = sizeScore
    float cnt = 1.0
    if useVolumeConfirm and not na(volRatioNow)
        sum := sum + volScore
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if useSmtConfluence
        sum := sum + smtScore
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if useM1Confirmation
        sum := sum + m1Score
        cnt := cnt + 1
    math.round(sum / cnt)

// finds the nearest untested liquidity pool beyond entryP in the trade's
// direction -- the actual "draw of liquidity" price is likely reaching for,
// not an arbitrary R-multiple. Bull looks in swingHighs above entry, bear
// looks in swingLows below entry; returns na if none exist yet. Requires
// s.touches >= minPoolTouches, not just s.isPool -- a level multiple prior
// swings have actually clustered at, not just the bare minimum first match.
findLiquidityTarget(string dir, float entryP) =>
    float best = na
    if dir == "bull"
        if array.size(swingHighs) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(swingHighs) - 1
                Swing s = array.get(swingHighs, i)
                if s.touches >= minPoolTouches and s.price > entryP
                    if na(best) or s.price < best
                        best := s.price
    else
        if array.size(swingLows) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(swingLows) - 1
                Swing s = array.get(swingLows, i)
                if s.touches >= minPoolTouches and s.price < entryP
                    if na(best) or s.price > best
                        best := s.price
    best

// finds up to the two nearest untested liquidity pools strictly between entryP
// and boundaryP (the final target) in the trade's direction -- real draws of
// liquidity for the TP1/TP2 ladder, not arbitrary percentage splits of the
// distance to target. Same minPoolTouches significance filter as
// findLiquidityTarget. Returns na for either/both if fewer than that many
// pools actually exist in range -- never fabricated.
findLiquidityLevels(string dir, float entryP, float boundaryP) =>
    float first = na
    float second = na
    if dir == "bull"
        if array.size(swingHighs) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(swingHighs) - 1
                Swing s = array.get(swingHighs, i)
                if s.touches >= minPoolTouches and s.price > entryP and s.price < boundaryP
                    if na(first) or s.price < first
                        second := first
                        first := s.price
                    else if na(second) or s.price < second
                        second := s.price
    else
        if array.size(swingLows) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(swingLows) - 1
                Swing s = array.get(swingLows, i)
                if s.touches >= minPoolTouches and s.price < entryP and s.price > boundaryP
                    if na(first) or s.price > first
                        second := first
                        first := s.price
                    else if na(second) or s.price > second
                        second := s.price
    [first, second]

// the actual target used for the webhook payload: nearest liquidity pool
// in the trade's direction, or the R-multiple projection if no pool exists
// yet (early session, thin swing history). Also returns which one it used
// so the payload can say so -- Polaris explains this back to Landen on the
// dashboard instead of just showing a bare number.
computeTarget(string dir, float entryP, float stopP) =>
    float poolTarget = findLiquidityTarget(dir, entryP)
    float fallback = dir == "bull" ? entryP + math.abs(entryP - stopP) * rMultiple : entryP - math.abs(entryP - stopP) * rMultiple
    bool usedPool = not na(poolTarget)
    [usedPool ? poolTarget : fallback, usedPool]

// ---------- killzone sessions ----------
// Computed here (ahead of the FVG/order-block/premium-discount markup below
// it in the original layout) because shouldFireSetup() needs inAnyKillzone
// and Pine doesn't hoist -- an identifier has to be declared above the code
// that reads it, not just above it in the same logical section.
inAsia   = not na(time(timeframe.period, asiaSession, "America/New_York"))
inLondon = not na(time(timeframe.period, londonSession, "America/New_York"))
inNyAm   = not na(time(timeframe.period, nyAmSession, "America/New_York"))
inNyPm   = not na(time(timeframe.period, nyPmSession, "America/New_York"))
bool inAnyKillzone = inAsia or inLondon or inNyAm or inNyPm
bgcolor(showKillzones and (inAsia or inLondon) ? color.new(#00D4FF, 95) : na, title="Asia/London killzone")
bgcolor(showKillzones and (inNyAm or inNyPm) ? color.new(#F5C86B, 95) : na, title="NY killzone")

// ---------- V2: setup detectors + master gate ----------
// Pine functions can only READ outer-scope state, never reassign it
// (CE10088) -- so every detector below is a pure function: it searches and
// returns what it found, but never touches seq*. The call site (top-level
// code in the main scan block) is what actually assigns seq* on a hit --
// same split already used for buildTradePlanDrawings above. Each returns
// [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] so the scan loop can treat every
// setup type the same way once more than one is real.

// detectSweep(dir) -- the existing (and currently only) entry trigger: best
// pool-eligible swing that got wicked through and closed back on the other
// side. Identical search to what used to be inline in the main scan block.
detectSweep(string dir) =>
    bool found = false
    float level = na
    float extreme = na
    float cisdTarget = na
    if dir == "bear" and array.size(swingHighs) > 0
        float bestHigh = na
        for i = 0 to array.size(swingHighs) - 1
            Swing s = array.get(swingHighs, i)
            if s.isPool and high > s.price and close < s.price
                if na(bestHigh) or s.price > bestHigh
                    bestHigh := s.price
        if not na(bestHigh)
            found := true
            level := bestHigh
            extreme := high
            cisdTarget := cisdTargetBear()
    else if dir == "bull" and array.size(swingLows) > 0
        float bestLow = na
        for i = 0 to array.size(swingLows) - 1
            Swing s = array.get(swingLows, i)
            if s.isPool and low < s.price and close > s.price
                if na(bestLow) or s.price < bestLow
                    bestLow := s.price
        if not na(bestLow)
            found := true
            level := bestLow
            extreme := low
            cisdTarget := cisdTargetBull()
    [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget]

// detectReversal(dir) -- a broader change-of-character trigger than
// detectSweep(): the single most recent swing (index 0), wicked through and
// closed back on the other side, WITHOUT requiring it to be a pool-eligible
// (equal-high/low) swing the way a sweep does. This is the actual coverage-
// gap fix -- sweep only fires on liquidity pools; reversal fires on any
// significant swing break. allowReversal defaults off, so this changes
// nothing until you opt in.
detectReversal(string dir) =>
    bool found = false
    float level = na
    float extreme = na
    float cisdTarget = na
    if dir == "bear" and array.size(swingHighs) > 0
        Swing s = array.get(swingHighs, 0)
        if high > s.price and close < s.price
            found := true
            level := s.price
            extreme := high
            cisdTarget := cisdTargetBear()
    else if dir == "bull" and array.size(swingLows) > 0
        Swing s = array.get(swingLows, 0)
        if low < s.price and close > s.price
            found := true
            level := s.price
            extreme := low
            cisdTarget := cisdTargetBull()
    [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget]

// detectContinuation(dir) -- a with-the-trend pullback trigger: fires when
// structureBias already agrees with dir (the trend is established, unlike
// sweep/reversal which require structure to actually break) and this bar is
// a fresh displacement candle in that same direction. level = this bar's
// own open (the near edge that must hold, mirroring how an order block's
// base is defined elsewhere in this script); extreme = this bar's opposite
// wick (the stop basis). Reuses cisdTargetBear/Bull() as-is -- it's a
// generic "find where the last opposite-colored run started" helper, not
// intrinsically tied to sweeps.
detectContinuation(string dir) =>
    bool found = false
    float level = na
    float extreme = na
    float cisdTarget = na
    if dir == "bear" and structureBias == "bear" and isDisplacement and close < open
        found := true
        level := open
        extreme := high
        cisdTarget := cisdTargetBear()
    else if dir == "bull" and structureBias == "bull" and isDisplacement and close > open
        found := true
        level := open
        extreme := low
        cisdTarget := cisdTargetBull()
    [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget]

// detectBreakout(dir) -- fires when a displacement candle closes decisively
// beyond the widest tracked swing on that side (the edge of the current
// range), i.e. genuine continuation through resistance/support rather than
// a sweep-and-reverse. level = that widest swing (support/resistance once
// broken -- closing back across it invalidates the sequence, same as every
// other entry trigger); extreme = this bar's opposite wick.
detectBreakout(string dir) =>
    bool found = false
    float level = na
    float extreme = na
    float cisdTarget = na
    if dir == "bull" and array.size(swingHighs) > 0 and isDisplacement and close > open
        float widestHigh = na
        for i = 0 to array.size(swingHighs) - 1
            Swing s = array.get(swingHighs, i)
            if na(widestHigh) or s.price > widestHigh
                widestHigh := s.price
        if not na(widestHigh) and close > widestHigh
            found := true
            level := widestHigh
            extreme := low
            cisdTarget := cisdTargetBull()
    else if dir == "bear" and array.size(swingLows) > 0 and isDisplacement and close < open
        float widestLow = na
        for i = 0 to array.size(swingLows) - 1
            Swing s = array.get(swingLows, i)
            if na(widestLow) or s.price < widestLow
                widestLow := s.price
        if not na(widestLow) and close < widestLow
            found := true
            level := widestLow
            extreme := high
            cisdTarget := cisdTargetBear()
    [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget]

// shouldFireSetup(setupType, dir) -- the master gate every candidate signal
// passes through before a detector even runs. Per-type on/off toggle, the
// bias/HTF/regime/session checks that started as inline bearAllowed/
// bullAllowed, plus Phase 2's gates: a stricter optional ADX floor, a
// volume floor, a minimum bar-range sanity check, and the contradiction
// filter (blocks a setup within minBarsAfterSetup of the last one that
// actually fired in the opposite direction -- the "buy signal, then sell
// signal 5 minutes later" problem). minSeqFvgSizeAtr is checked separately,
// at the 4 completion sites, since it depends on that specific sequence's
// FVG, not something shouldFireSetup has visibility into at the sweep stage.
shouldFireSetup(string setupType, string dir) =>
    bool typeAllowed = setupType == "sweep" ? allowSweep : setupType == "reversal" ? allowReversal : setupType == "continuation" ? allowContinuation : setupType == "breakout" ? allowBreakout : false
    bool biasOk = dir == "bear" ? structureBias != "bull" : structureBias != "bear"
    bool htfOk = not useHtfBias or (dir == "bear" ? htfBias != "bull" : htfBias != "bear")
    bool sessionOk = not useSessionFilter or inAnyKillzone
    bool adxOk = not raiseAdxThreshold or adxVal >= raisedAdxThreshold
    bool volFloorOk = not useVolFloor or na(volRatio) or volRatio >= volFloorMult
    bool rangeOk = minBarRangeAtr <= 0 or (high - low) >= minBarRangeAtr * atrVal
    bool contradictionOk = not useContradictionFilter or na(lastSetupDir) or lastSetupDir == dir or (bar_index - lastSetupBar) >= minBarsAfterSetup
    typeAllowed and biasOk and htfOk and regimeOk and sessionOk and adxOk and volFloorOk and rangeOk and contradictionOk

// maps seqTriggerType + direction to one of the setupType strings
// functions/index.js's VALID_SETUP_TYPES already accepts and index.html's
// setupTypeLabel() already translates to plain English -- both were built
// ahead of this wiring, back when every completed sequence just reported
// "CHoCH_DOWN"/"CHoCH_UP" regardless of what actually triggered it. Sweep
// keeps the literal liquidity-sweep label; reversal keeps CHoCH (a change
// of character on a non-pool swing is still a change of character);
// continuation and breakout both map to BOS -- a genuine break of
// structure either way, and VALID_SETUP_TYPES has no separate "breakout"
// slot to add without also touching the Cloud Function's allow-list.
setupTypeForTrigger(string trigger, string dir) =>
    bool isDown = dir == "bear"
    trigger == "sweep" ? (isDown ? "LIQUIDITY_SWEEP_SELL" : "LIQUIDITY_SWEEP_BUY") :
     trigger == "reversal" ? (isDown ? "CHoCH_DOWN" : "CHoCH_UP") :
     (isDown ? "BOS_DOWN" : "BOS_UP")

// ---------- webhook payload builders ----------
// "kind" discriminates the two payload shapes this script ever sends -- the
// Cloud Function branches on it (see functions/index.js): "setup" is a full
// completed setup (-> alerts collection, AI-reviewed, can SMS); "status" is
// a lightweight phase-transition ping (-> a single overwritten Firestore
// doc, no history, purely so the dashboard/Polaris knows what the indicator
// is currently tracking between full setups).
buildAlertMessage(string setupType, float entryPrice, float stopPrice, float targetPrice, int confidence, bool targetIsPool) =>
    float risk = math.abs(entryPrice - stopPrice)
    float reward = math.abs(targetPrice - entryPrice)
    float rr = risk > 0 ? math.round((reward / risk) * 100) / 100 : na
    '{"secret":"' + webhookSecret + '","kind":"setup","setupType":"' + setupType + '","entryPrice":' + str.tostring(entryPrice) +
     ',"stopPrice":' + str.tostring(stopPrice) + ',"targetPrice":' + str.tostring(targetPrice) +
     ',"confidence":' + str.tostring(confidence) + ',"riskReward":' + str.tostring(rr) +
     ',"targetSource":"' + (targetIsPool ? "pool" : "fallback") + '"' +
     ',"symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","timeframe":"' + timeframe.period + '"}'

// wins/losses ride along on every status ping (not just alert completion) so
// the dashboard's win-rate readout stays current even mid-sequence, not just
// the instant a setup fires -- cheap to include, they're already tracked.
buildStatusMessage() =>
    string regimeTxt = regimeOk ? "trend" : "chop"
    string biasTxt = na(structureBias) ? "none" : structureBias
    string htfTxt = na(htfBias) ? "none" : htfBias
    string phaseTxt = na(seqPhase) ? "idle" : seqPhase
    string dirTxt = na(seqDir) ? "none" : seqDir
    '{"secret":"' + webhookSecret + '","kind":"status","structureBias":"' + biasTxt + '","htfBias":"' + htfTxt +
     '","regime":"' + regimeTxt + '","adx":' + str.tostring(adxVal, "#.##") + ',"phase":"' + phaseTxt +
     '","dir":"' + dirTxt + '","wins":' + str.tostring(scoreWins) + ',"losses":' + str.tostring(scoreLosses) +
     ',"symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","timeframe":"' + timeframe.period + '"}'

// Pine functions cannot reassign a global-scope variable (CE10088) -- only
// top-level script code can. So these two helpers only ever READ the tp*
// globals or act on values passed in as parameters; every actual `:=` to a
// tp* global happens at the call site instead (see the 4 completion sites
// below, and the "clear the tracked trade plan" block).
deleteLineIfExists(line ln) =>
    if not na(ln)
        line.delete(ln)

deleteLabelIfExists(label lb) =>
    if not na(lb)
        label.delete(lb)

// deletes whatever trade-plan drawings are currently tracked (reads the tp*
// globals, mutates nothing) -- called both when a new plan replaces an old
// one and when the tracked plan is invalidated.
clearTradePlanDrawings() =>
    deleteLineIfExists(tpEntryLine)
    deleteLineIfExists(tpStopLine)
    deleteLineIfExists(tpTargetLine)
    deleteLineIfExists(tp1Line)
    deleteLineIfExists(tp2Line)
    deleteLabelIfExists(tpEntryLbl)
    deleteLabelIfExists(tpStopLbl)
    deleteLabelIfExists(tpTargetLbl)
    deleteLabelIfExists(tp1Lbl)
    deleteLabelIfExists(tp2Lbl)
    deleteLabelIfExists(tpSetupLbl)

// builds the entry/stop/target trade-plan drawings for a just-completed
// setup and returns their handles -- the call site is responsible for
// clearing the previously-tracked plan first and assigning these into the
// tp* globals (a plain function can't do either of those itself). When
// showTpLadder is on, also draws TP1/TP2 at the nearest real liquidity pools
// between entry and the final target (findLiquidityLevels) -- not arbitrary
// percentage splits of the distance to target. If fewer than two such pools
// actually exist, only that many lines are drawn (never fabricated) --
// visual only either way, doesn't touch the webhook payload, scorecard, or
// targetP itself, which all still resolve against the one real target.
buildTradePlanDrawings(string dir, float entryP, float stopP, float targetP, int conf) =>
    string confText = showConfidence ? "\n" + str.tostring(conf) + "%" : ""
    string setupText = dir == "bull" ? "▲ LONG SETUP" + confText : "▼ SHORT SETUP" + confText
    color setupColor = dir == "bull" ? #2FE08A : #FF5566
    int lineEnd = bar_index + lineExtension
    label setupLbl = label.new(bar_index, dir == "bull" ? high : low, setupText, style=dir == "bull" ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=setupColor, textcolor=#030710, size=size.normal)
    line entryLine = line.new(bar_index, entryP, lineEnd, entryP, color=#00D4FF, style=line.style_solid, width=2)
    line stopLine = line.new(bar_index, stopP, lineEnd, stopP, color=#FF5566, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
    line targetLine = line.new(bar_index, targetP, lineEnd, targetP, color=#2FE08A, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
    label entryLbl = label.new(lineEnd, entryP, "ENTRY " + str.tostring(entryP, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#0B1626, 10), textcolor=#00D4FF, size=size.small)
    label stopLbl = label.new(lineEnd, stopP, "STOP " + str.tostring(stopP, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#0B1626, 10), textcolor=#FF5566, size=size.small)
    label targetLbl = label.new(lineEnd, targetP, "TARGET " + str.tostring(targetP, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#0B1626, 10), textcolor=#2FE08A, size=size.small)
    // Pine ternaries can't return tuples (CE10163) -- findLiquidityLevels() returns
    // one, so this has to be an if/else assigning into pre-declared na floats
    // instead of the ternary pattern used everywhere else in this function.
    float tp1Price = na
    float tp2Price = na
    if showTpLadder
        [t1, t2] = findLiquidityLevels(dir, entryP, targetP)
        tp1Price := t1
        tp2Price := t2
    line newTp1Line = showTpLadder and not na(tp1Price) ? line.new(bar_index, tp1Price, lineEnd, tp1Price, color=color.new(#2FE08A, 60), style=line.style_dotted, width=1) : line(na)
    line newTp2Line = showTpLadder and not na(tp2Price) ? line.new(bar_index, tp2Price, lineEnd, tp2Price, color=color.new(#2FE08A, 40), style=line.style_dotted, width=1) : line(na)
    label newTp1Lbl = showTpLadder and not na(tp1Price) ? label.new(lineEnd, tp1Price, "TP1 " + str.tostring(tp1Price, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#0B1626, 10), textcolor=color.new(#2FE08A, 40), size=size.small) : label(na)
    label newTp2Lbl = showTpLadder and not na(tp2Price) ? label.new(lineEnd, tp2Price, "TP2 " + str.tostring(tp2Price, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#0B1626, 10), textcolor=color.new(#2FE08A, 20), size=size.small) : label(na)
    [setupLbl, entryLine, stopLine, targetLine, entryLbl, stopLbl, targetLbl, newTp1Line, newTp2Line, newTp1Lbl, newTp2Lbl]

// ---------- order blocks (last opposing candle before a displacement move) ----------
if showOB and barstate.isconfirmed and isDisplacement
    if close > open and (not obBiasFilter or structureBias != "bear")
        int k = 1
        bool found = false
        while k <= obLookback and not found
            if close[k] < open[k]
                found := true
                box ob = box.new(bar_index - k, top=open[k], right=bar_index + 15, bottom=close[k], border_color=color.new(#2FE08A, 45), bgcolor=color.new(#2FE08A, 88), extend=extend.none, text="OB", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.new(#2FE08A, 10))
                array.unshift(obBoxes, ob)
                if array.size(obBoxes) > maxOB
                    box.delete(array.pop(obBoxes))
            k += 1
    else if close < open and (not obBiasFilter or structureBias != "bull")
        int k = 1
        bool found = false
        while k <= obLookback and not found
            if close[k] > open[k]
                found := true
                box ob = box.new(bar_index - k, top=close[k], right=bar_index + 15, bottom=open[k], border_color=color.new(#FF5566, 45), bgcolor=color.new(#FF5566, 88), extend=extend.none, text="OB", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.new(#FF5566, 10))
                array.unshift(obBoxes, ob)
                if array.size(obBoxes) > maxOB
                    box.delete(array.pop(obBoxes))
            k += 1

// ---------- fair value gaps everywhere (not just inside an active sequence) ----------
if showAllFvg and barstate.isconfirmed
    [hasBull, bLo, bHi] = fvgAtBull(0)
    if hasBull and (bHi - bLo) >= minFvgSizeAtr * atrVal
        box fb = box.new(bar_index - 2, top=bHi, right=bar_index + 20, bottom=bLo, border_color=color.new(#2FE08A, 35), bgcolor=color.new(#2FE08A, 88), extend=extend.none, text="FVG", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.new(#2FE08A, 10))
        array.unshift(fvgBoxes, fb)
        array.unshift(fvgBoxLo, bLo)
        array.unshift(fvgBoxHi, bHi)
        array.unshift(fvgBoxDir, "bull")
        array.unshift(fvgBoxDone, false)
        if array.size(fvgBoxes) > maxFvgBoxes
            box.delete(array.pop(fvgBoxes))
            array.pop(fvgBoxLo)
            array.pop(fvgBoxHi)
            array.pop(fvgBoxDir)
            array.pop(fvgBoxDone)

    [hasBear, brLo, brHi] = fvgAtBear(0)
    if hasBear and (brHi - brLo) >= minFvgSizeAtr * atrVal
        box fb2 = box.new(bar_index - 2, top=brHi, right=bar_index + 20, bottom=brLo, border_color=color.new(#FF5566, 35), bgcolor=color.new(#FF5566, 88), extend=extend.none, text="FVG", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.new(#FF5566, 10))
        array.unshift(fvgBoxes, fb2)
        array.unshift(fvgBoxLo, brLo)
        array.unshift(fvgBoxHi, brHi)
        array.unshift(fvgBoxDir, "bear")
        array.unshift(fvgBoxDone, false)
        if array.size(fvgBoxes) > maxFvgBoxes
            box.delete(array.pop(fvgBoxes))
            array.pop(fvgBoxLo)
            array.pop(fvgBoxHi)
            array.pop(fvgBoxDir)
            array.pop(fvgBoxDone)

    // maintenance pass, newest-to-oldest so removals never skip an entry:
    // un-flipped zones flip to iFVG once violated; already-flipped zones get
    // deleted outright once price reclaims the whole zone back the other way
    // (the iFVG is no longer relevant once that happens)
    if array.size(fvgBoxes) > 0
        for i = array.size(fvgBoxes) - 1 to 0
            bool done = array.get(fvgBoxDone, i)
            string d = array.get(fvgBoxDir, i)
            float zLo = array.get(fvgBoxLo, i)
            float zHi = array.get(fvgBoxHi, i)
            box zb = array.get(fvgBoxes, i)
            if not done
                if showIfvg
                    bool violated = d == "bull" ? close < zLo : close > zHi
                    if violated
                        box.set_border_color(zb, color.new(#F5C86B, 20))
                        box.set_bgcolor(zb, color.new(#F5C86B, 85))
                        box.set_text(zb, "iFVG")
                        box.set_text_color(zb, color.new(#F5C86B, 10))
                        box.set_right(zb, bar_index + 20)
                        array.set(fvgBoxDone, i, true)
            else
                bool reclaimed = d == "bull" ? close > zHi : close < zLo
                if reclaimed
                    box.delete(zb)
                    array.remove(fvgBoxes, i)
                    array.remove(fvgBoxLo, i)
                    array.remove(fvgBoxHi, i)
                    array.remove(fvgBoxDir, i)
                    array.remove(fvgBoxDone, i)

// ---------- premium / discount zone (around the active swing range) ----------
if showPD and barstate.isconfirmed and array.size(swingHighs) > 0 and array.size(swingLows) > 0
    Swing hiS = array.get(swingHighs, 0)
    Swing loS = array.get(swingLows, 0)
    if hiS.price > loS.price
        float eq = (hiS.price + loS.price) / 2
        int leftX = math.min(hiS.idx, loS.idx)
        if not na(premiumBox)
            box.delete(premiumBox)
        if not na(discountBox)
            box.delete(discountBox)
        if not na(eqLine)
            line.delete(eqLine)
        premiumBox := box.new(leftX, top=hiS.price, right=bar_index + 10, bottom=eq, border_color=color.new(#FF5566, 75), bgcolor=color.new(#FF5566, 94), extend=extend.none, text="PREMIUM", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.new(#FF5566, 30))
        discountBox := box.new(leftX, top=eq, right=bar_index + 10, bottom=loS.price, border_color=color.new(#2FE08A, 75), bgcolor=color.new(#2FE08A, 94), extend=extend.none, text="DISCOUNT", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.new(#2FE08A, 30))
        eqLine := line.new(leftX, eq, bar_index + 10, eq, color=color.new(#F5C86B, 40), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)

// ---------- per-session volatility tracking ----------
// runs every confirmed bar regardless of showKillzones/useSessionFilter --
// this is a pure readout, not a gate. On every session change, folds the
// just-completed session's realized range into that session's running
// average; while still inside a session, extends the running high/low.
if showSessionVolatility and barstate.isconfirmed
    string nowSession = inAsia ? "asia" : inLondon ? "london" : inNyAm ? "nyam" : inNyPm ? "nypm" : na
    if nowSession != curSession
        if not na(curSession) and not na(curSessionHigh) and not na(curSessionLow)
            float completedRange = curSessionHigh - curSessionLow
            if curSession == "asia"
                sumRangeAsia := sumRangeAsia + completedRange
                countAsia := countAsia + 1
            else if curSession == "london"
                sumRangeLondon := sumRangeLondon + completedRange
                countLondon := countLondon + 1
            else if curSession == "nyam"
                sumRangeNyAm := sumRangeNyAm + completedRange
                countNyAm := countNyAm + 1
            else if curSession == "nypm"
                sumRangeNyPm := sumRangeNyPm + completedRange
                countNyPm := countNyPm + 1
        curSession := nowSession
        curSessionHigh := na(nowSession) ? na : high
        curSessionLow := na(nowSession) ? na : low
    else if not na(nowSession)
        curSessionHigh := math.max(curSessionHigh, high)
        curSessionLow := math.min(curSessionLow, low)

// ---------- clear the tracked trade plan once it's played out ----------
// an entry that already hit its stop or target shouldn't linger on the
// chart looking live -- top-level code (not a function) so it can actually
// clear tpActive itself.
if barstate.isconfirmed and tpActive
    bool tpStopped = tpDir == "bull" ? low <= tpStop : high >= tpStop
    bool tpReached = tpDir == "bull" ? high >= tpTarget : low <= tpTarget
    if tpStopped or tpReached
        clearTradePlanDrawings()
        tpActive := false

// ---------- scorecard: resolve pending signals against price ----------
// runs before the main scan so a signal recorded THIS bar (entry = this
// bar's close) never gets checked against this same bar's high/low --
// resolution only starts from the next bar onward.
if showScorecard and barstate.isconfirmed and array.size(pendingDir) > 0
    for i = array.size(pendingDir) - 1 to 0
        string pDir = array.get(pendingDir, i)
        float pEntry = array.get(pendingEntry, i)
        float pStop = array.get(pendingStop, i)
        float pTarget = array.get(pendingTarget, i)
        bool hitStop = pDir == "bull" ? low <= pStop : high >= pStop
        bool hitTarget = pDir == "bull" ? high >= pTarget : low <= pTarget
        if hitStop or hitTarget
            // conservative tie-break: if a single wide bar could have
            // touched both, we can't know which came first intrabar, so
            // it counts as a loss rather than assuming the favorable order
            if hitTarget and not hitStop
                scoreWins := scoreWins + 1
                // a win pays out THIS trade's real reward:risk, not a fixed
                // amount -- risk is what actually happened at entry, so this
                // is real realized R, not the minRiskReward floor
                float riskAtEntry = math.abs(pEntry - pStop)
                if riskAtEntry > 0
                    sumR := sumR + math.abs(pTarget - pEntry) / riskAtEntry
            else
                scoreLosses := scoreLosses + 1
                // a loss always costs exactly -1R by definition -- it
                // resolved at the stop, i.e. the full risked distance
                sumR := sumR - 1.0
            array.remove(pendingDir, i)
            array.remove(pendingEntry, i)
            array.remove(pendingStop, i)
            array.remove(pendingTarget, i)

// ---------- main scan (mirrors advanceScan), only on confirmed/closed bars ----------
if barstate.isconfirmed
    string prevPhase = seqPhase  // snapshot before this bar's transitions, for the status ping below
    if na(seqDir)
        // Entry triggers, checked in order -- first one to actually find
        // something starts the sequence. Each is independently gated by
        // shouldFireSetup(type, dir) (which includes the per-type
        // allowSweep/allowReversal/allowContinuation/allowBreakout toggle),
        // so with only allowSweep on by default this reduces to exactly the
        // old sweep-only behavior. seqSmtAligned captures this sequence's
        // SMT reading once, at trigger time, for setupConfidence() to use
        // later regardless of how many bars pass before it actually fires.
        if shouldFireSetup("sweep", "bear")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectSweep("bear")
            if found
                seqDir := "bear"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBearDiv
                seqTriggerType := "sweep"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, high, "⚡ SWEEP", style=label.style_label_down, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

        if na(seqDir) and shouldFireSetup("reversal", "bear")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectReversal("bear")
            if found
                seqDir := "bear"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBearDiv
                seqTriggerType := "reversal"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, high, "⚡ REVERSAL", style=label.style_label_down, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

        if na(seqDir) and shouldFireSetup("continuation", "bear")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectContinuation("bear")
            if found
                seqDir := "bear"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBearDiv
                seqTriggerType := "continuation"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, high, "⚡ CONTINUATION", style=label.style_label_down, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

        if na(seqDir) and shouldFireSetup("breakout", "bear")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectBreakout("bear")
            if found
                seqDir := "bear"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBearDiv
                seqTriggerType := "breakout"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, high, "⚡ BREAKOUT", style=label.style_label_down, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

        if na(seqDir) and shouldFireSetup("sweep", "bull")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectSweep("bull")
            if found
                seqDir := "bull"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBullDiv
                seqTriggerType := "sweep"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, low, "⚡ SWEEP", style=label.style_label_up, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

        if na(seqDir) and shouldFireSetup("reversal", "bull")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectReversal("bull")
            if found
                seqDir := "bull"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBullDiv
                seqTriggerType := "reversal"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, low, "⚡ REVERSAL", style=label.style_label_up, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

        if na(seqDir) and shouldFireSetup("continuation", "bull")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectContinuation("bull")
            if found
                seqDir := "bull"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBullDiv
                seqTriggerType := "continuation"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, low, "⚡ CONTINUATION", style=label.style_label_up, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

        if na(seqDir) and shouldFireSetup("breakout", "bull")
            [found, level, extreme, cisdTarget] = detectBreakout("bull")
            if found
                seqDir := "bull"
                seqPhase := "sweep"
                seqLevel := level
                seqSweepExtreme := extreme
                seqCisdTarget := cisdTarget
                seqSweepBar := bar_index
                seqHasFvg := false
                seqSmtAligned := smtBullDiv
                seqTriggerType := "breakout"
                if showVisuals
                    label.new(bar_index, low, "⚡ BREAKOUT", style=label.style_label_up, color=#F5C86B, textcolor=#030710, size=size.small)

    else
        if bar_index - seqSweepBar > maxBarsValid
            seqDir := na
            seqPhase := na
        else if seqDir == "bear"
            if seqPhase == "sweep"
                if close > seqLevel
                    seqDir := na
                    seqPhase := na
                else if close < seqCisdTarget
                    int barsSince = bar_index - seqSweepBar
                    bool found = false
                    float fLo = na
                    float fHi = na
                    for off = 0 to math.min(barsSince - 1, 200)
                        if not found
                            [has, lo, hi] = fvgAtBear(off)
                            if has
                                found := true
                                fLo := lo
                                fHi := hi
                    seqPhase := "cisd"
                    seqHasFvg := found
                    seqFvgLo := fLo
                    seqFvgHi := fHi
            else if seqPhase == "cisd"
                if not seqHasFvg
                    [has, lo, hi] = fvgAtBear(0)
                    if has
                        seqHasFvg := true
                        seqFvgLo := lo
                        seqFvgHi := hi
                    else if close > seqLevel
                        seqDir := na
                        seqPhase := na
                if seqHasFvg and not na(seqDir)
                    if close > seqFvgHi
                        seqDir := na
                        seqPhase := na
                    else if high >= seqFvgLo
                        if close < seqFvgLo
                            int conf = setupConfidence(seqFvgLo, seqFvgHi, atrVal, volRatio, seqSmtAligned, seqDir == "bear" ? m1RejectionBear : m1RejectionBull)
                            float entryP = close
                            float stopP = seqSweepExtreme + stopBufferPts + (useWickTolerance ? wickToleranceAtr * atrVal : 0.0)
                            [targetP, targetIsPool] = computeTarget("bear", entryP, stopP)
                            float riskPts = math.abs(entryP - stopP)
                            float rewardPts = math.abs(targetP - entryP)
                            bool rrOk = minRiskReward <= 0 or (riskPts > 0 and (rewardPts / riskPts) >= minRiskReward)
                            if rewardPts >= minTargetAtrMult * atrVal and rewardPts >= minTargetPts and rrOk and (seqFvgHi - seqFvgLo) >= minSeqFvgSizeAtr * atrVal
                                alert(buildAlertMessage(setupTypeForTrigger(seqTriggerType, "bear"), entryP, stopP, targetP, conf, targetIsPool), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                                lastSetupDir := "bear"
                                lastSetupBar := bar_index
                                if showScorecard
                                    array.unshift(pendingDir, "bear")
                                    array.unshift(pendingEntry, entryP)
                                    array.unshift(pendingStop, stopP)
                                    array.unshift(pendingTarget, targetP)
                                    if array.size(pendingDir) > maxPending
                                        array.pop(pendingDir)
                                        array.pop(pendingEntry)
                                        array.pop(pendingStop)
                                        array.pop(pendingTarget)
                                if showTradePlan
                                    clearTradePlanDrawings()
                                    [newSetupLbl, newEntryLine, newStopLine, newTargetLine, newEntryLbl, newStopLbl, newTargetLbl, newTp1Line, newTp2Line, newTp1Lbl, newTp2Lbl] = buildTradePlanDrawings("bear", entryP, stopP, targetP, conf)
                                    tpSetupLbl := newSetupLbl
                                    tpEntryLine := newEntryLine
                                    tpStopLine := newStopLine
                                    tpTargetLine := newTargetLine
                                    tpEntryLbl := newEntryLbl
                                    tpStopLbl := newStopLbl
                                    tpTargetLbl := newTargetLbl
                                    tp1Line := newTp1Line
                                    tp2Line := newTp2Line
                                    tp1Lbl := newTp1Lbl
                                    tp2Lbl := newTp2Lbl
                                    tpDir := "bear"
                                    tpStop := stopP
                                    tpTarget := targetP
                                    tpActive := true
                            seqDir := na
                            seqPhase := na
                        else
                            seqPhase := "retrace"
            else if seqPhase == "retrace"
                if close > seqFvgHi
                    seqDir := na
                    seqPhase := na
                else if close < seqFvgLo
                    int conf = setupConfidence(seqFvgLo, seqFvgHi, atrVal, volRatio, seqSmtAligned, seqDir == "bear" ? m1RejectionBear : m1RejectionBull)
                    float entryP = close
                    float stopP = seqSweepExtreme + stopBufferPts + (useWickTolerance ? wickToleranceAtr * atrVal : 0.0)
                    [targetP, targetIsPool] = computeTarget("bear", entryP, stopP)
                    float riskPts = math.abs(entryP - stopP)
                    float rewardPts = math.abs(targetP - entryP)
                    bool rrOk = minRiskReward <= 0 or (riskPts > 0 and (rewardPts / riskPts) >= minRiskReward)
                    if rewardPts >= minTargetAtrMult * atrVal and rewardPts >= minTargetPts and rrOk and (seqFvgHi - seqFvgLo) >= minSeqFvgSizeAtr * atrVal
                        alert(buildAlertMessage(setupTypeForTrigger(seqTriggerType, "bear"), entryP, stopP, targetP, conf, targetIsPool), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                        lastSetupDir := "bear"
                        lastSetupBar := bar_index
                        if showScorecard
                            array.unshift(pendingDir, "bear")
                            array.unshift(pendingEntry, entryP)
                            array.unshift(pendingStop, stopP)
                            array.unshift(pendingTarget, targetP)
                            if array.size(pendingDir) > maxPending
                                array.pop(pendingDir)
                                array.pop(pendingEntry)
                                array.pop(pendingStop)
                                array.pop(pendingTarget)
                        if showTradePlan
                            clearTradePlanDrawings()
                            [newSetupLbl, newEntryLine, newStopLine, newTargetLine, newEntryLbl, newStopLbl, newTargetLbl, newTp1Line, newTp2Line, newTp1Lbl, newTp2Lbl] = buildTradePlanDrawings("bear", entryP, stopP, targetP, conf)
                            tpSetupLbl := newSetupLbl
                            tpEntryLine := newEntryLine
                            tpStopLine := newStopLine
                            tpTargetLine := newTargetLine
                            tpEntryLbl := newEntryLbl
                            tpStopLbl := newStopLbl
                            tpTargetLbl := newTargetLbl
                            tp1Line := newTp1Line
                            tp2Line := newTp2Line
                            tp1Lbl := newTp1Lbl
                            tp2Lbl := newTp2Lbl
                            tpDir := "bear"
                            tpStop := stopP
                            tpTarget := targetP
                            tpActive := true
                    seqDir := na
                    seqPhase := na
        else if seqDir == "bull"
            if seqPhase == "sweep"
                if close < seqLevel
                    seqDir := na
                    seqPhase := na
                else if close > seqCisdTarget
                    int barsSince = bar_index - seqSweepBar
                    bool found = false
                    float fLo = na
                    float fHi = na
                    for off = 0 to math.min(barsSince - 1, 200)
                        if not found
                            [has, lo, hi] = fvgAtBull(off)
                            if has
                                found := true
                                fLo := lo
                                fHi := hi
                    seqPhase := "cisd"
                    seqHasFvg := found
                    seqFvgLo := fLo
                    seqFvgHi := fHi
            else if seqPhase == "cisd"
                if not seqHasFvg
                    [has, lo, hi] = fvgAtBull(0)
                    if has
                        seqHasFvg := true
                        seqFvgLo := lo
                        seqFvgHi := hi
                    else if close < seqLevel
                        seqDir := na
                        seqPhase := na
                if seqHasFvg and not na(seqDir)
                    if close < seqFvgLo
                        seqDir := na
                        seqPhase := na
                    else if low <= seqFvgHi
                        if close > seqFvgHi
                            int conf = setupConfidence(seqFvgLo, seqFvgHi, atrVal, volRatio, seqSmtAligned, seqDir == "bear" ? m1RejectionBear : m1RejectionBull)
                            float entryP = close
                            float stopP = seqSweepExtreme - stopBufferPts - (useWickTolerance ? wickToleranceAtr * atrVal : 0.0)
                            [targetP, targetIsPool] = computeTarget("bull", entryP, stopP)
                            float riskPts = math.abs(entryP - stopP)
                            float rewardPts = math.abs(targetP - entryP)
                            bool rrOk = minRiskReward <= 0 or (riskPts > 0 and (rewardPts / riskPts) >= minRiskReward)
                            if rewardPts >= minTargetAtrMult * atrVal and rewardPts >= minTargetPts and rrOk and (seqFvgHi - seqFvgLo) >= minSeqFvgSizeAtr * atrVal
                                alert(buildAlertMessage(setupTypeForTrigger(seqTriggerType, "bull"), entryP, stopP, targetP, conf, targetIsPool), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                                lastSetupDir := "bull"
                                lastSetupBar := bar_index
                                if showScorecard
                                    array.unshift(pendingDir, "bull")
                                    array.unshift(pendingEntry, entryP)
                                    array.unshift(pendingStop, stopP)
                                    array.unshift(pendingTarget, targetP)
                                    if array.size(pendingDir) > maxPending
                                        array.pop(pendingDir)
                                        array.pop(pendingEntry)
                                        array.pop(pendingStop)
                                        array.pop(pendingTarget)
                                if showTradePlan
                                    clearTradePlanDrawings()
                                    [newSetupLbl, newEntryLine, newStopLine, newTargetLine, newEntryLbl, newStopLbl, newTargetLbl, newTp1Line, newTp2Line, newTp1Lbl, newTp2Lbl] = buildTradePlanDrawings("bull", entryP, stopP, targetP, conf)
                                    tpSetupLbl := newSetupLbl
                                    tpEntryLine := newEntryLine
                                    tpStopLine := newStopLine
                                    tpTargetLine := newTargetLine
                                    tpEntryLbl := newEntryLbl
                                    tpStopLbl := newStopLbl
                                    tpTargetLbl := newTargetLbl
                                    tp1Line := newTp1Line
                                    tp2Line := newTp2Line
                                    tp1Lbl := newTp1Lbl
                                    tp2Lbl := newTp2Lbl
                                    tpDir := "bull"
                                    tpStop := stopP
                                    tpTarget := targetP
                                    tpActive := true
                            seqDir := na
                            seqPhase := na
                        else
                            seqPhase := "retrace"
            else if seqPhase == "retrace"
                if close < seqFvgLo
                    seqDir := na
                    seqPhase := na
                else if close > seqFvgHi
                    int conf = setupConfidence(seqFvgLo, seqFvgHi, atrVal, volRatio, seqSmtAligned, seqDir == "bear" ? m1RejectionBear : m1RejectionBull)
                    float entryP = close
                    float stopP = seqSweepExtreme - stopBufferPts - (useWickTolerance ? wickToleranceAtr * atrVal : 0.0)
                    [targetP, targetIsPool] = computeTarget("bull", entryP, stopP)
                    float riskPts = math.abs(entryP - stopP)
                    float rewardPts = math.abs(targetP - entryP)
                    bool rrOk = minRiskReward <= 0 or (riskPts > 0 and (rewardPts / riskPts) >= minRiskReward)
                    if rewardPts >= minTargetAtrMult * atrVal and rewardPts >= minTargetPts and rrOk and (seqFvgHi - seqFvgLo) >= minSeqFvgSizeAtr * atrVal
                        alert(buildAlertMessage(setupTypeForTrigger(seqTriggerType, "bull"), entryP, stopP, targetP, conf, targetIsPool), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                        lastSetupDir := "bull"
                        lastSetupBar := bar_index
                        if showScorecard
                            array.unshift(pendingDir, "bull")
                            array.unshift(pendingEntry, entryP)
                            array.unshift(pendingStop, stopP)
                            array.unshift(pendingTarget, targetP)
                            if array.size(pendingDir) > maxPending
                                array.pop(pendingDir)
                                array.pop(pendingEntry)
                                array.pop(pendingStop)
                                array.pop(pendingTarget)
                        if showTradePlan
                            clearTradePlanDrawings()
                            [newSetupLbl, newEntryLine, newStopLine, newTargetLine, newEntryLbl, newStopLbl, newTargetLbl, newTp1Line, newTp2Line, newTp1Lbl, newTp2Lbl] = buildTradePlanDrawings("bull", entryP, stopP, targetP, conf)
                            tpSetupLbl := newSetupLbl
                            tpEntryLine := newEntryLine
                            tpStopLine := newStopLine
                            tpTargetLine := newTargetLine
                            tpEntryLbl := newEntryLbl
                            tpStopLbl := newStopLbl
                            tpTargetLbl := newTargetLbl
                            tp1Line := newTp1Line
                            tp2Line := newTp2Line
                            tp1Lbl := newTp1Lbl
                            tp2Lbl := newTp2Lbl
                            tpDir := "bull"
                            tpStop := stopP
                            tpTarget := targetP
                            tpActive := true
                    seqDir := na
                    seqPhase := na

    // fires a lightweight status ping whenever the phase actually advanced
    // this bar (na->sweep, sweep->cisd, cisd->retrace) -- not on invalidation
    // or completion (seqPhase going back to na), since a real "setup" alert
    // already covers completion with far richer detail.
    if seqPhase != prevPhase and not na(seqPhase)
        alert(buildStatusMessage(), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ---------- tracked level line while a sequence is active ----------
if showVisuals and not na(seqPhase)
    line.new(seqSweepBar, seqLevel, bar_index, seqLevel, color=color.new(#F5C86B, 55), style=line.style_dashed, width=1)

// ---------- status HUD (top-right) ----------
var table hud = table.new(position=position.top_right, columns=2, rows=12, bgcolor=color.new(#0B1626, 8), border_color=color.new(#00D4FF, 45), border_width=1, frame_color=color.new(#00D4FF, 45), frame_width=1)

if showHud and barstate.islast
    // "BIAS" row doubles as the direction row -- structureBias IS the direction
    // reading once useMtfDirection is on (see the swing-detection block above), so
    // this is a single row with a label that names its actual source, not two rows
    // showing the same value.
    string biasLabel = useMtfDirection ? "DIR " + directionTimeframe : "BIAS"
    table.cell(hud, 0, 0, "◆ POLARIS", text_color=#F5C86B, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 0, "SCANNER", text_color=#F5C86B, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 1, biasLabel, text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 1, na(structureBias) ? "--" : (structureBias == "bull" ? "▲ LONG" : "▼ SHORT"), text_color=na(structureBias) ? #6E93AD : (structureBias == "bull" ? #2FE08A : #FF5566), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 2, "HTF " + htfTimeframe, text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 2, na(htfBias) ? "--" : (htfBias == "bull" ? "▲ LONG" : "▼ SHORT"), text_color=na(htfBias) ? #6E93AD : (htfBias == "bull" ? #2FE08A : #FF5566), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 3, "ADX", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 3, str.tostring(adxVal, "#.#") + (regimeOk ? " TREND" : " CHOP"), text_color=regimeOk ? #DDF3FF : #6E93AD, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 4, "PHASE", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 4, na(seqPhase) ? "IDLE" : str.upper(seqPhase), text_color=na(seqPhase) ? #6E93AD : #DDF3FF, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 5, "SETUP", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 5, na(seqDir) ? "--" : (seqDir == "bull" ? "▲ LONG" : "▼ SHORT"), text_color=na(seqDir) ? #6E93AD : (seqDir == "bull" ? #2FE08A : #FF5566), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    string sessionName = inAsia ? "ASIA" : inLondon ? "LONDON" : inNyAm ? "NY AM" : inNyPm ? "NY PM" : "--"
    float sessionAvg = inAsia ? (countAsia > 0 ? sumRangeAsia / countAsia : na) : inLondon ? (countLondon > 0 ? sumRangeLondon / countLondon : na) : inNyAm ? (countNyAm > 0 ? sumRangeNyAm / countNyAm : na) : inNyPm ? (countNyPm > 0 ? sumRangeNyPm / countNyPm : na) : na
    string sessionTxt = sessionName == "--" ? "--" : sessionName + (na(sessionAvg) ? "" : " · avg " + str.tostring(sessionAvg, format.mintick))
    table.cell(hud, 0, 6, "SESSION", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 6, sessionTxt, text_color=sessionName == "--" ? #6E93AD : #DDF3FF, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    if useVolumeConfirm
        table.cell(hud, 0, 7, "VOL", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
        table.cell(hud, 1, 7, na(volRatio) ? "--" : str.tostring(volRatio, "#.##") + "x avg", text_color=na(volRatio) ? #6E93AD : (volRatio >= 1.2 ? #2FE08A : #DDF3FF), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    if useSmtConfluence
        string smtTxt = smtBearDiv ? "BEAR DIV" : smtBullDiv ? "BULL DIV" : "--"
        table.cell(hud, 0, 8, "SMT", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
        table.cell(hud, 1, 8, smtTxt, text_color=smtTxt == "--" ? #6E93AD : #F5C86B, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    if useM1Confirmation
        string m1Txt = m1RejectionBear ? "BEAR REJ" : m1RejectionBull ? "BULL REJ" : "--"
        table.cell(hud, 0, 9, "M1", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
        table.cell(hud, 1, 9, m1Txt, text_color=m1Txt == "--" ? #6E93AD : #F5C86B, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
    if showScorecard
        int totalResolved = scoreWins + scoreLosses
        string scoreTxt = totalResolved > 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(scoreWins / totalResolved * 100)) + "% (" + str.tostring(scoreWins) + "/" + str.tostring(totalResolved) + ")" : "-- (0/0)"
        table.cell(hud, 0, 10, "SCORE", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
        table.cell(hud, 1, 10, scoreTxt, text_color=totalResolved > 0 and scoreWins / totalResolved >= 0.5 ? #2FE08A : #DDF3FF, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
        // the number that actually says whether this is working -- win% alone
        // can't tell a 35%-win-at-3R system (great) from a 65%-win-at-1.2R one
        // (bad). Real average R-multiple per resolved trade, not win count.
        float avgR = totalResolved > 0 ? sumR / totalResolved : na
        string expTxt = na(avgR) ? "--" : (avgR >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(avgR, "#.##") + "R"
        table.cell(hud, 0, 11, "EXP", text_color=#6E93AD, text_size=size.tiny, text_halign=text.align_left)
        table.cell(hud, 1, 11, expTxt, text_color=na(avgR) ? #6E93AD : (avgR >= 0 ? #2FE08A : #FF5566), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)
